<p>An explosion and fire at a fireworks store in Donghai County in China’s eastern Jiangsu province killed eight people and injured two, according to state media reports carried by multiple outlets. The blast happened during the Lunar New Year holiday period, when many people use fireworks as part of traditional celebrations. Several reports cited state broadcaster CCTV, which said fireworks had been set off near the shop. After the blast, China’s Ministry of Emergency Management held an emergency meeting and urged local officials to prevent similar incidents, underscoring the added safety pressure during the holiday period.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/3GFbnVNSgaxarnPWFsC-pHM9tLQeDXknmczUr61rIf1hQsu0aUuvbIzkY-L7kRFJNdA7WklZiVWBscWfQOgO7um2thQDw21_ALfrKJS2X5jzcn7vwm1S0TJbhwF0LNvdM-KRPpljiuV3FlJQA2m7DNmagt00X7M0e64_oHIMiaho0CziSQZV' alt='A view of the aftermath of a reported fireworks-store blast in Jiangsu province, China.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>More precise location: Reports put the fireworks shop in Dongan village in Donghai County, Jiangsu province.</li><li>Holiday timing: The blast happened on the first day of China’s nine-day Lunar New Year holiday, when fireworks use typically surges.</li><li>Cause described in reports: A villager allegedly set off fireworks improperly near the store shortly before the explosion.</li><li>Broader risk warning: Authorities warned that safety risks often rise ahead of Lunar New Year as fireworks use increases.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Ministry of Emergency Management (China): After the blast, the ministry held an emergency meeting and told officials they needed to prevent similar incidents during the holiday period. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3343684/8-dead-fireworks-shop-blast-start-chinas-lunar-new-year-holiday'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>CCTV (state broadcaster): CCTV linked the incident to fireworks being set off near the store, according to reports. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3343684/8-dead-fireworks-shop-blast-start-chinas-lunar-new-year-holiday'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Xinhua (state news agency): Xinhua described an explosion followed by a fire at a fireworks store in Donghai County, Jiangsu. (<a href='https://english.news.cn/20260215/793ffe5cdb0a4431aa14202751921779/c.html'>Xinhua</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.thehindu.com/news/international/china-fireworks-store-explosion-monday-february-16/article70637420.ece'>A fireworks store explosion in China kills 8 ahead of Lunar New Year</a> - thehindu.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/china/politics/article/3343684/8-dead-fireworks-shop-blast-start-chinas-lunar-new-year-holiday'>8 dead in fireworks shop blast at start of China’s Lunar New Year holiday</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.firstpost.com/world/at-least-8-killed-2-injured-in-fireworks-store-explosion-in-eastern-china-13980171.html'>At least 8 killed, 2 injured in fireworks store explosion in eastern China</a> - firstpost.com</li><li><a href='https://english.news.cn/20260215/793ffe5cdb0a4431aa14202751921779/c.html'>Eight people are killed and two others are injured in an explosion and fire at a fireworks store in Donghai County, Jiangsu, China.</a> - news.cn</li></ul>